{"id": "section-body-04254", "title": "Viral Keratoconjunctivitis (VKC)", "chapterId": "chapter-four", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "NOTIFIABLE DISEASES", "Viral Infections", "Viral Keratoconjunctivitis (VKC)"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-04254", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Viral Keratoconjunctivitis (VKC)", "runs": [{"text": "Viral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Keratoconjunctivitis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(VKC)"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1802"}}, {"id": "body-04255", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "It is a viral eye infection accounting for over 80% of cases of epidemic keratoconjunctivitis (EKC)/Red eye with more than 75% attributed specifically to adenovirus infection. Epidemic keratoconjunctivitis (EKC) is an eye condition primarily characterized by dilation of the conjunctival blood vessels (hyperemia), conjunctival edema (chemosis), and ocular discharge. It may be unilateral but usually bilateral.", "runs": [{"text": "It"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "viral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "eye"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infection"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "accounting"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "over"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "80%"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cases"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "epidemic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "keratoconjunctivitis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(EKC)/Red"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "eye"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "more"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "than"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "75% attributed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "specifically"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "adenovirus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infection."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Epidemic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "keratoconjunctivitis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(EKC)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "an"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "eye"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "condition"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "primarily"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "characterized by dilation of the conjunctival blood vessels (hyperemia), conjunctival edema (chemosis), and ocular discharge. It may be unilateral but usually bilateral."}]}, {"id": "body-04257", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Adenovirus serotypes Ad 5, 8, 11, 13, 19, and 37 are frequently implicated in outbreaks of EKC and are known to cause severe conjunctivitis. Adenoviruses are highly resilient, capable of surviving on inanimate surfaces for up to 30 days, which contributes significantly to their potential for widespread transmission.", "runs": [{"text": "Adenovirus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "serotypes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Ad"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "5,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "8,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "11,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "13,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "19,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "37"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "frequently"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "implicated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "outbreaks"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "EKC"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "known"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cause"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "severe conjunctivitis."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Adenoviruses"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "highly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "resilient,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "capable"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "surviving"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inanimate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "surfaces"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "up"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "30"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "days,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "which"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "contributes significantly to their potential for widespread transmission."}]}, {"id": "body-04259", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "The incubation period for adenoviral EKC ranges from 2 to 14 days, with most individuals developing signs and symptoms within 5 to 6 days’ post-exposure. Importantly, viral shedding can occur in asymptomatic individuals, and infected persons may remain contagious for 10 to 14 days after symptom onset, posing a substantial risk for community and healthcare-associated transmission.", "runs": [{"text": "The incubation period for adenoviral EKC ranges from 2 to 14 days, with most individuals developing signs and symptoms within"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "5"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "6"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "days’"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "post-exposure."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Importantly,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "viral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "shedding"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "occur"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "asymptomatic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "individuals,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "persons"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may remain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "contagious"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "10"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "14"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "days"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "after"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "symptom"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "onset,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "posing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "substantial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "risk"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "community"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "healthcare-associated "}, {"text": "transmission."}]}, {"id": "body-04262", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04263", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A typical case of VKC is presented by:", "runs": [{"text": "A"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "typical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "VKC"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "presented"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by:"}]}, {"id": "body-04264", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Conjunctival injection (redness).", "runs": [{"text": "Conjunctival"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "injection"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(redness)."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1765"}}, {"id": "body-04265", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Follicular conjunctivitis (small, raised bumps on the conjunctiva).", "runs": [{"text": "Follicular conjunctivitis (small, raised bumps on the conjunctiva)."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1765"}}, {"id": "body-04266", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Preauricular lymphadenopathy (swollen lymph nodes near the ear).", "runs": [{"text": "Preauricular lymphadenopathy (swollen lymph nodes near the ear)."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1765"}}, {"id": "body-04267", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Corneal involvement (e.g., subepithelial infiltrates or epithelial keratitis) in severe cases.", "runs": [{"text": "Corneal involvement (e.g., subepithelial infiltrates"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "epithelial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "keratitis)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in severe cases."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1765"}}, {"id": "body-04268", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Pseudo membrane formation in epidemic keratoconjunctivitis (EKC), a severe adenoviral form.", "runs": [{"text": "Pseudo membrane formation in epidemic keratoconjunctivitis (EKC), a severe adenoviral "}, {"text": "form."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1765"}}, {"id": "body-04269", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Transmission", "runs": [{"text": "Transmission"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04272", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Acute onset of unilateral or bilateral red eyes.", "runs": [{"text": "Acute"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "onset"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "unilateral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bilateral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "red"}, {"text": " eyes."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1764"}}, {"id": "body-04273", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Watery or mucoid discharge.", "runs": [{"text": "Watery"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mucoid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "discharge."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1764"}}, {"id": "body-04274", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Foreign body sensation, burning, or itching.", "runs": [{"text": "Foreign"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "body"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sensation,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "burning,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "itching."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1764"}}, {"id": "body-04275", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Photophobia (sensitivity to light) in cases with corneal involvement (keratitis).", "runs": [{"text": "Photophobia (sensitivity to light) in cases with corneal involvement (keratitis)."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1764"}}, {"id": "body-04276", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Possible associated upper respiratory symptoms (e.g., sore throat, fever) due to systemic viral infection.", "runs": [{"text": "Possible associated upper respiratory symptoms (e.g., sore throat, fever) due to systemic viral infection."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1764"}}, {"id": "body-04278", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Epidemic viral keratoconjunctivitis/Red eye is very contagious and mostly spread from human to human or inanimate objects to human through hand-to-eye contact by hands or objects that are contaminated with the virus. Other ways include contact with: Infectious tears, Eye discharge, Fecal matter, Respiratory discharge and large respiratory tract droplets.", "runs": [{"text": "Epidemic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "viral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "keratoconjunctivitis/Red"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "eye"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "very"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "contagious"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mostly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "spread"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "from"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "human"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "human"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inanimate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "objects to human through hand-to-eye contact by hands or objects that are contaminated with the virus. Other ways include contact with: Infectious tears, Eye discharge, Fecal matter, Respiratory discharge and large respiratory tract droplets."}]}, {"id": "body-04280", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Case definitions", "runs": [{"text": "Case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "definitions"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04281", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Suspected Case: Any person presenting with acute red eye with watery discharge and without an alternative diagnosis (e.g., bacterial conjunctivitis or allergy) OR with history of exposure to a confirmed case or outbreak setting (e.g., schools, hospitals) within 7-14 days.", "runs": [{"text": "Suspected Case:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Any"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "person presenting with acute red eye with watery"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "discharge and without"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "an alternative diagnosis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(e.g., bacterial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "conjunctivitis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "allergy)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "OR"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "history"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "exposure"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "confirmed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "outbreak"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "setting"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(e.g.,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "schools,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hospitals) within 7-14 days."}]}, {"id": "body-04283", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Probable Case: A suspected case with clinical signs like follicular conjunctivitis or preauricular lymphadenopathy with epidemiological link (e.g., contact with a confirmed case).", "runs": [{"text": "Probable Case: ", "bold": true}, {"text": "A suspected case with clinical signs like follicular conjunctivitis or preauricular lymphadenopathy with epidemiological link (e.g., contact with a confirmed case)."}]}, {"id": "body-04285", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Confirmed Case: A suspected or probable case with a laboratory confirmation (e.g., positive PCR or immunochromatography for adenovirus).", "runs": [{"text": "Confirmed", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Case:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "A"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "suspected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "probable"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "laboratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "confirmation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(e.g.,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "positive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "PCR"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "immunochromatography for adenovirus)."}]}, {"id": "body-04287", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Differential Diagnosis", "runs": [{"text": "Differential"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Diagnosis"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04288", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "The above case definitions distinguish VKC from:", "runs": [{"text": "The"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "above"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "definitions"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "distinguish"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "VKC"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "from:"}]}, {"id": "body-04289", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Bacterial conjunctivitis which presents with purulent discharge without follicular response.", "runs": [{"text": "Bacterial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "conjunctivitis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "which"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "presents"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "purulent"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "discharge"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "without"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "follicular"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "response."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1763"}}, {"id": "body-04290", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Allergic conjunctivitis which presents with itching, seasonal, without lymphadenopathy.", "runs": [{"text": "Allergic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "conjunctivitis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "which"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "presents"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "itching,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "seasonal,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "without"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lymphadenopathy."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1763"}}, {"id": "body-04291", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Herpes simplex virus (HSV) which present with keratitis (dendritic corneal lesions, unilateral).", "runs": [{"text": "Herpes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "simplex"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "virus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(HSV)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "which"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "present"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "keratitis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(dendritic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "corneal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lesions,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "unilateral)."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1763"}}, {"id": "body-04293", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Complications", "runs": [{"text": "Complications"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04294", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Persistent corneal infiltrates or secondary bacterial infections may require additional treatments, such as antibiotics for superinfections.", "runs": [{"text": "Persistent"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "corneal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infiltrates"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "secondary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bacterial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infections"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "require"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "additional"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "treatments,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "such"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "antibiotics for superinfections."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1763"}}, {"id": "body-04295", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Severe cases with vision-threatening complications need urgent ophthalmology referral.", "runs": [{"text": "Severe"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cases"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "vision-threatening"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "complications"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "need"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "urgent"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ophthalmology"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "referral."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1763"}}, {"id": "body-04295-textbox1-00001", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Note:", "runs": [{"text": "Note:", "bold": true}]}, {"id": "body-04295-textbox1-00002", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Treatment is nonspecific, mainly is supportive and symptoms relief, preventing complications, and limiting spread, as there is no specific antiviral cure for most cases. Most cases resolve in 1-3 weeks without specific treatment.", "runs": [{"text": "Treatment"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "nonspecific,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mainly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "supportive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "symptoms"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "relief,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "preventing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "complications,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "limiting"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "spread, as there is no specific antiviral cure for most cases. Most cases resolve in 1-3 weeks without specific treatment."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1762"}}, {"id": "body-04295-textbox1-00003", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Topical Antihistamines or Decongestants: For itching or redness. Use cautiously to avoid rebound redness.", "runs": [{"text": "Topical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Antihistamines"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Decongestants:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "For"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "itching"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "redness."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Use"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cautiously"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "avoid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rebound"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "redness."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1762"}}, {"id": "body-04295-textbox1-00004", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Topical NSAIDs: In cases with significant discomfort or photophobia, s